  "bounded_findings": [
    "For private and three-file multi edits, whole-branch candidate/main paired-ratio medians are approximately 0.419/0.350 in check and 0.772/0.827 in O2. Private check is faster in 5/6 pairs; multi check and both O2 edit cases are faster in 6/6 pairs.",
    "O2 unchanged regresses in 4/6 pairs, paired ratio median approximately 1.128. O2 broad edit is essentially neutral: 3/6 faster, paired ratio median approximately 0.996. No all-scenario or workload-frequency-weighted improvement is established.",
    "Cold/check and several small cells have visible round-to-round variation; all six observations remain. Ratio of arm medians, median of paired ratios and paired geometric mean are distinct statistics and must not be substituted selectively.",
    "Actual current object count is 16 in all successful native arms, but partition membership and invalidation differ. Zil private/multi hits are 15/14; Rust physical carry-forward is 15/13. Carry-forward identifies inode/device/mtime/content continuity, not direct rustc query-color counters.",
    "All 2064 Zil object-hit receipts still run current machine preflight and report no native Builder/optimization/emission. Private-edit raw reports still execute Verify, Lower and Link. There is substantial work after local cache reuse.",
    "One block private-edit defined T/t symbols per object differ markedly: Zil [23,23,42,42,42,42,21,21,21,21,21,21,21,21,21,21] versus Rust [1,2,2,1,1,1,1,1,1,3,1,2,2,2,4,2]. These are emitted symbol observations, not source function counts. Matching requested and actual CGU16 does not equalize optimizer work or partition bodies.",
    "All six Rust unchanged requests are Cargo Fresh with no rustc invocation; Zil successful requests retain mandatory current Verify. Their unchanged timings describe different workflows and assurance costs.",
    "Native main/candidate LLVM text and ELF are identical for all 78 successful pairs, and 2808 actual native process outcomes match exact bytes/exit oracles. This supports main/candidate code-output preservation for this workload, not a Rust runtime-performance comparison.",
    "Current main-to-candidate differences include the entire research branch, not isolated attribution to the serialization slice. Profile counters show avoided encoding traversals, but full byte assembly/hash/write/fsync and semantic publication remain."
  ],
